# H1: hand the cards back to production. The LAST job of the window and it runs even when any earlier job failed, stalled or hung: the status of every board, the all-four reset, the fabric re-measure
# (it must pass before production serves), then the node agent starts again with NOTHING placed. The agent serves the rig daemon's local :latest, which this window did NOT move; an owner /deploy is still
# needed, always, to place TODAY'S PRODUCTION RECIPE (c2-packed-tp4). NEVER place a gate arm or this window's image. This job never includes a deploy, a :latest retag or a placement call.
# If the fabric re-measure fails the job stops before agentstart: production stays down until a board is healed. Duration (estimate): 25 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/gluefix window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/gluefix and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-gluefix-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for ONE FRESH tag (never used before) that B0 builds from the pushed tp4/gluefix commit while production
# serves; the driver substitutes it in every template. A reused tag is skipped by the build step and would silently serve an old image.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset fabric agentstart
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-gluefix-1
